I am Legend is about a zombie-like horde  wiping out much of humanity but it's  confusing ending and butterfly symbolism  become a lot more clear if you  understand the personal journey of its  hero created by genetically altering  measles the cryptid virus seemed like a  miracle cure unfortunately after its  initial promise the virus mutates with  catastrophic results the virus kills 5.4  billion people with 5% transformed into  zombie or vampire like dark seekers 1%  of the population remains immune which  includes Neville a viral adjust for the  u.s. army played by Will Smith Neville  remains in New York City after it is  placed in military quarantine  although Neville is nearly entirely  alone in New York he still got his  faithful dog Sam for company although  Neville's world-saving quest to create  an antidote gives him long-term purpose  his nurturing and caring for Sam give  him a reason to continue in the daily  basis Sam provides immediate meaning a  series of flashbacks slowly reveal  events before the quarantine  contextualizing Neville's mind set these  flashbacks depict the critical moment  Neville evacuates his wife Zoey and  daughter Marlene then tragedy strikes  when another helicopter collides with  Zoey and Marley's helicopter killing  them shortly before her death Neville  had promised Marley that he would make  the monsters go away it becomes clear  from that point that present-day Neville  is seeking personal salvation and  finding the cure not only for the future  of humanity but also so his family's  death won't be in vain the death of Zoey  and Marley also explains Sam's value  from that moment on sand becomes a  living remnant of nevels old life the  only family member he can love and care  for Bob Marley song three little birds  is intertwined with the theme of I am  Legend the song stands for belief at a  brighter future and inspires neville in  times of need it also facilitates a form  of cathartic escapism the guard's  Neville from insanity his daughter was  named after the cultural icon implying  that long before the end of world events  the original Marley was an inspiration  for Neville a conversation at one point  with fellow survivor Anna near the end  of the film even suggests that Neville  chose his career as a biologist thanks  to Marlon while talking to Anna  Neville says he had this idea it was  kind of a virologists idea he believed  that you could cure racism and hate  literally cure it by injecting music and  love into people's lives in an act of  revenge for trapping a dark seeker for  his tests Neville falls into a trap and  is ambushed by other dark seekers  including canines also infected with the  virus after escaping to the safety of  his home Neville realizes his dog Sam is  infected unlike her owner Sam isn't  immune from the virus in a scene that  would melt the coldest of hearts Neville  is forced to strangle his best friend  and only companion Sam's death alone  doesn't break Neville  it's everything her death represents  she's the tie to his past life a daily  reminder of his motivation to find  Redemption and a buffer between being  alone and experiencing suffocating  loneliness rationality is replaced by  rage when Neville embarks on a suicidal  act of revenge just as Neville is about  to become an evening snack a beam of  light scares the dark seekers away after  three years with no response to his  radio broadcast another face of humanity  has finally arrived however rather than  express gratitude for saving him Neville  is dismissive and struggles to  communicate every single person that you  or I has ever known is dead as I am  Legend reaches its climax the situation  becomes desperate when  large group of dark seekers invade  nevels home Nevel Anna and Ethan flee to  the basement laboratory for safety there  they discover that Neville's antidote is  finally working the dark seekers make  their way to the left with one taking  lead and smashing himself into the glass  partition when the leader smashes  himself into the glass the cracks  resemble a butterfly taking notice at  the butterfly tattoo on Anna's neck  Neville has a realization that this  might indeed be divine intervention this  connects to a gesture from Neville's  daughter Marly earlier in the film  Neville understands this is no  coincidence  after a moment of realization Neville  takes action he draws blood containing  the cure from the dark secret test  subject and gives it to Anna and her son  after seeing that his efforts to make a  cure weren't in vain Neville is now  comfortable paying the ultimate hero  sacrifice to save Anna and even after  Neville's selfless final act Anna and  Ethan make it to the colony and hand  over the vial containing the cure  Neville has become the titular legend in  the alternate ending of I am Legend the  themes of the story are drastically  changed the dark seeker alpha wipes his  own blood onto the glass in the shape of  a butterfly  Neville then turns to the dark seeker  test subject on his table the one he's  cured and notices a butterfly tattoo on  her neck  Neville takes a leap of faith and opens  the glass partition risking his life to  reunite the dark seekers once Neville's  awakened the female the two dark seekers  embrace in a moment of surprising  humanity Smith's character realizes that  the mutants are able to express love and  are closer to humanity than he realized  from the dark seekers perspective  Neville preyed on them kidnapping and  experimenting on their friends family  and loved ones he's a legend but for the  wrong reasons in line with the original  book he has become the monstrous legend  of a new world check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos about your favorite movies  are coming soon subscribe to our YouTube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]
 

